  "implemented": [
    "A fresh counted contributor inventory retains every visited child identity, serialized order, class/version and containing hierarchy separately from frozen V1-V5 recovery profiles.",
    "Complete source-track audition requires every counted child of one direct audio track to be a supported retained event with matching source provenance and attached media. Unknown, missing, repeated, nested, removed or extra contributors cannot become partial complete-track output.",
    "Chronological disjoint canonical ranges and native reader windows compose in original counted order using the saved CPR clock. Gaps, event boundaries and seeks use the existing direct reader with each file rate retained and no implicit rate conversion.",
    "The collector contract explicitly uses fresh root mode 0, fresh zero event flags/attributes and nil external predicate. This is a named reconstruction context, not restored hosted Cubase state.",
    "Shared immutable source placement context avoids repeated clock reconstruction while preserving the single-event arithmetic and source-owner checks. Each media hash, full source capacity and aggregate sample budget is checked before transport installation.",
    "The app exposes complete-track inspection/admission, event count and transport identity while keeping editable-project playback guarded and historical source/report files unchanged."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Complete counted source membership is not complete channel or project acoustic fidelity. Mixer, routing, inserts, sends, automation, nested containers and unknown contributors remain outside this named source audition.",
    "Unsorted or overlapping ranges, unresolved priority/normalization, explicit fades and effective automatic fades are not admitted. Source order is not silently sorted or repaired.",
    "Fresh root/filter/attribute state does not establish hosted post-read callbacks, registry mutation, effective engine rate or device state.",
    "Symbolic multi-event controls have self-authored minimal ancillary bodies. They test app parsing and sample composition, not native-valid CPR restoration or Cubase output.",
    "Different saved/source clocks retain raw source-frame consumption and can change speed and pitch. No automatic resampler or missing-frame padding is introduced.",
    "Own implementation tests and GUI/engine observations are not DAC capture, native callback equivalence or Cubase runtime comparison. Full product fidelity remains incomplete."
  ]
